// trap: a true rule whose proof needs a ∀∃ lemma (#428): every order in one state has a
// child in another. Prepare readies an order only while it has a sent shipment, Finish
// closes a ready order with no guard, and nothing deletes a shipment or unsends one, so
// every done order has a sent shipment, at any count. The rule is not inductive alone: from
// a ready order with no sent shipment, which no reachable state has, Finish breaks it. The
// fact that rules that state out, "every ready order has a sent shipment", says a row
// exists; every mined lemma is universal, so z3 leaves the rule unproved, and BFS finds
// nothing. The fact is also a count of the order's children (at least one sent shipment);
// z3_needs_exists_global.rdra needs one over rows no key links.
// expect Quantifier_Order_0: native=ok tlc=ok z3=unproved bfs=ok,ok,ok
// expect Deadlock_Order_status_open: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample
entity Order "注文" { id: Int @pk  status: Enum(open, ready, done) @default(open) }
entity Shipment "出荷" { id: Int @pk  status: Enum(packed, sent) @default(packed) }
relate(Shipment, Order, N:1)
usecase Place "注文"
usecase Pack "梱包"
usecase Send "発送"
usecase Prepare "準備完了"
usecase Finish "完了"
creates(Place, Order)
creates(Pack, Shipment)
updates(Pack, Order)
transitions(Send, Shipment.status, packed -> sent)
transitions(Prepare, Order.status, open -> ready)
transitions(Finish, Order.status, ready -> done)
condition Sent "発送済みの出荷がある"
holds(Sent, Order.status == open).has(Shipment.status == sent)
applies_to(Sent, Prepare)
invariant(Order).when(status == done).has(Shipment.status == sent)
